  "content": {
    "id": "p14-q15-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "15",
    "prompt": "Suppose that 210 unit square tiles are arranged without overlap into a rectangular shape.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p14-q15-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "What is the smallest perimeter that the rectangle can have?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$58$ units.\n\nThe closest factor pair of $210$ is $14$ and $15$.",
          "worked": "$$210=2\\times3\\times5\\times7.$$\nThe possible side lengths, in units, are the factor pairs\n$$(1,210),\\ (2,105),\\ (3,70),\\ (5,42),\\ (6,35),\\ (7,30),\\ (10,21),\\ (14,15).$$\nTheir sums are $211,107,73,47,41,37,31,29$, respectively. The smallest sum is $29$, for sides $14$ and $15$.\n$$\\begin{align*}P&=2(14+15)\\\\P&=58\\text{ units}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 60
      },
      {
        "id": "p14-q15-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Given that the perimeter of the rectangle is 62, find its dimensions.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$10$ units by $21$ units.",
          "worked": "The side lengths have product $210$ and sum $62\\div2=31$. From the factor pairs of $210$, the pair with sum $31$ is $10$ and $21$.\n$$\\begin{align*}10\\times21&=210,\\\\2(10+21)&=62.\\end{align*}$$\nThe dimensions are $10$ units by $21$ units.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      }
    ]
  },
